From 330ae24d56f852ec3b3569ef2012dc0ce13362f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:10:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] OpenEuiccService: Implement profile metadata lookup and
 download

Carrier apps (and anything else using the public EuiccManager API)
download profiles through EuiccService, but OpenEuiccService never
implemented onDownloadSubscription() and only returned a stub from
onGetDownloadableSubscriptionMetadata().

- onGetDownloadableSubscriptionMetadata(): run the ES9+ session up to
  AuthenticateClient to obtain the profile metadata, then abort it.
  Report the carrier name and the carrier privilege access rules to the
  platform, which checks them against the calling app before allowing
  an unprivileged app to download (after the user consented).
- onDownloadSubscription(): download via the existing foreground
  download task (notifications, progress) and, for
  switchAfterDownload, enable the new profile afterwards. Returns
  RESULT_RESOLVABLE_ERRORS/CONFIRMATION_CODE if the activation code
  requires a confirmation code that was not supplied, and
  RESULT_MUST_DEACTIVATE_SIM if no eUICC port is mapped and the
  platform did not allow deactivating a SIM.
- hidden-apis-stub/shim: add the port-aware EuiccService overloads and
  reflection shims for the eUICC system APIs used (Gradle build only;
  the AOSP build uses the real APIs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
